# Form Configuration

This guide explains how to configure your RSVP form to collect the information you need from guests.

## Accessing the Form Builder

To configure your RSVP form:

1. Navigate to your event
2. Open the **Settings** tab or **RSVP Form** section
3. You'll see the form builder interface

## Section Management

### Enabling/Disabling Sections

Each of the four sections can be turned on or off:

1. Find the section in the builder
2. Toggle the switch to enable or disable it
3. Disabled sections won't appear on the guest form

{% callout type="info" %}
The Personal Information section is always visible with at least the RSVP response options.
{% /callout %}

### Section Descriptions

Add custom descriptions to each section to provide context for guests. Descriptions support both English and Arabic.

## Field Configuration

### Enabling Standard Fields

Within each section, toggle individual fields on or off:

1. Find the field in the section
2. Click the toggle to enable or disable it
3. Only enabled fields appear on the form

### Required vs Optional

Mark fields as required to ensure guests provide the information:

1. Enable the field
2. Check the **Required** checkbox
3. Guests must complete required fields before submitting

### Category-Specific Visibility

Show certain fields only to specific guest categories:

1. Enable the field
2. Click **Category Visibility**
3. Select which categories can see this field
4. Unselected categories won't see the field

{% callout type="info" %}
Use category visibility to ask VIP guests different questions than standard guests.
{% /callout %}

## Standard Fields Reference

### Logistics Section

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Arrival Date | Date picker | When the guest arrives |
| Departure Date | Date picker | When the guest leaves |
| Arrival Flight | Text | Incoming flight number |
| Departure Flight | Text | Outgoing flight number |
| Hotel Required | Yes/No | Whether accommodation is needed |
| Hotel Check-in | Date picker | Check-in date (if hotel required) |
| Hotel Check-out | Date picker | Check-out date (if hotel required) |
| Transport Required | Yes/No | Whether airport pickup is needed |

### Important to Know Section

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Dietary Type | Dropdown | Vegetarian, Vegan, Halal, etc. |
| Dietary Details | Text area | Allergies and specifics |
| Accessibility Type | Dropdown | Wheelchair, hearing, visual, etc. |
| Accessibility Details | Text area | Specific needs |
| Emergency Contact Name | Text | Emergency contact person |
| Emergency Contact Phone | Text | Emergency contact number |

### Personal Section

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| Preferred Language | Dropdown | English or Arabic |

## Conditional Fields

Some fields appear based on other responses:

- **Hotel Check-in/Check-out** - Only shown if "Hotel Required" is "Yes"
- **Dietary Details** - Only shown if "Dietary Type" is not "None"
- **Accessibility Details** - Only shown if "Accessibility Type" is not "None"

This keeps the form clean by hiding irrelevant questions.

## Saving Changes

Form configuration changes are saved automatically. Guests who access their RSVP link will see the updated form immediately.

{% callout type="warning" %}
Be careful when removing fields after guests have started responding. Existing responses are preserved, but you won't be able to collect that data from new respondents.
{% /callout %}
